## The loop (do not skip steps)
For each unchecked task in `tasks.md`:
1. Set `.agent/STATUS.md` to `state: implementing`, `task: N`. Write tests for the task's requirements first, then the code. Run the lane's tests, `ruff`, and `make contracts`. Commit `feat({{LANE}}): task N <title>`.
2. Set `state: in-review`. {{REVIEW_STEP}}
3. Read the review file. Fix every blocker and major finding (`state: fixing`, increment `round`). Keep or add a test for each. Commit `fix({{LANE}}): task N round K`.
4. Get the reviewer to re-review the delta. On `APPROVE`, tick the task's box in `tasks.md` and add a line to `.agent/LOG.md` (task, rounds, minutes).
5. After 3 rounds without approval: set `state: blocked`, record what is unresolved in `.agent/QUESTIONS.md`, and move to the next independent task.

When every task is ticked: write `docs/lanes/{{LANE}}.md`, finalize the `accept-{{LANE}}` recipe in `make/lane-{{LANE}}.mk` exactly as the spec's acceptance task describes, set `state: lane-review`, and run the lane review from the protocol. Stop when it approves and set `state: lane-done`.

## Non-negotiables
Validate every document at every boundary. Fail closed. Deterministic output. No network in tests (cassette LLM client, in-memory bus and store). Synthetic data only. Never weaken a test to get green. Never claim a task is done without a passing test for each of its requirements. Be concise in your messages: report state transitions and blockers, not narration.

